# Link-checker exclusions shared by Content Guard (changed posts only) and the
# weekly Link Audit (whole site). One regular expression per line.
#
# Hosts that permanently reject GitHub runner probes belong here. A site
# that is down for a while must NOT be added: Content Guard no longer checks
# old posts, and the weekly audit is the place to report it.

# Rate-limits or blocks runner IPs (429/403) although the pages are public.
scientificamerican\.com
techxplore\.com
nasa\.gov
security\.googleblog\.com
biorxiv\.org
openai\.com
technologyreview\.com
# Bot challenge (403) for any non-browser client.
ipcc\.ch
# APS DOIs resolve to journals.aps.org, which answers 403 to runner IPs; the DOI
# is the canonical, permanent identifier of the source.
doi\.org/10\.1103

# Specific sources returned 403 to the GitHub runner on 2026-11-03. These
# exceptions also affect the weekly audit and require separate manual review.
